# Strict cross-origin isolation on EVERY response of the docs site (house rule).
# `_headers` is honored by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. The CI publishes to GitHub Pages,
# which does NOT support custom headers, so these are INERT there — a reviewed trade-off:
# the runnable cells run a capability-DENIED pure-compute wasm contained by wasm isolation
# (not by COOP/COEP), and the single-threaded compiler needs no cross-origin isolation. These
# headers are kept so deploying the SAME bundle to a `_headers`-honoring host (or behind a
# header-setting proxy) restores strict isolation with no change.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
